<section class="band" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="letter">
      <h2 class="h2" id="story-h">Built because we needed it ourselves.</h2>
      <p>I run <strong>Ticket Spot</strong>, an event ticketing app sold on Shopify, Wix and Stripe. Each platform reports revenue its own way, so "what's our MRR?" meant three dashboards and a spreadsheet.</p>
      <p>The harder question was <strong>why organizers were leaving</strong>. By the time a cancellation arrived, they had usually stopped creating events weeks earlier, and we rarely heard why.</p>
      <p>OneMRR solves both in one product: one number for revenue you can explain, and a way to notice when customers drift and follow up while it still matters.</p>
      <div class="sig">
        <span class="mono" aria-hidden="true">CM</span>
        <span><b>Chris McCaw</b><br />Founder of OneMRR and Ticket Spot</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
